    <briefdescription>
<para>Leaky bucket traffic shaper. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Models a bucket with a fixed capacity that drains at a constant rate (<computeroutput>drain_rate_bps</computeroutput> bits per second). Data is added to the bucket via <computeroutput>add(bytes)</computeroutput>. If the bucket is full, <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1network_1_1_leaky_bucket_1abd5162e551115c66ae925a3317dcbdb8" kindref="member">add()</ref></computeroutput> returns false (overflow).</para>
<para>Unlike the <ref refid="classthemis_1_1network_1_1_token_bucket" kindref="compound">TokenBucket</ref>, the <ref refid="classthemis_1_1network_1_1_leaky_bucket" kindref="compound">LeakyBucket</ref> enforces a strict constant output rate with no accumulation — burst traffic is smoothed out.</para>
<para>Thread-safe via an internal mutex. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
